column13:
Publisher field is sometimes conflated with the resource "Creator" field. While it's not always apparent who the creator of the dataset is, the agent publishing the dataset to the open platforms is generally known. DublinCore cannot handle hierarchical provenance chain for multiple publishers. DCAT exposes qualifiedAttribution field that takes care of intra-ministerial departments with separate 'roles' in dataset publishing. Example [a prov:Attribution ;
prov:agent <http://example.org/organizations/nic-data-collector> ; # Link to the Data Collector agent
dcat:hadRole ex:dataCollector/dataCurator/dataSteward ; # Specify the role using dcat:hadRole and a custom vocabulary]

